;; The POSIX layer of the libraries' C (HE5, HES11 (a)): unix's, directory's, process's, time's and base's calls that
;; crt's kernel does not emulate (it has no chmod, links, utimes, directory streams, users, processes), over Go's os
;; and syscall packages on the host's files, paths resolved against the program's working directory. Files crt opened
;; are its fds (numbers below hfdBase); the pipes of a spawned process are this file's (hfdBase and above), read,
;; written and closed here, the calls on fds going to the one that owns the number.

